course: dictionary
lesson: 8875
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and shot is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they give you clues.
explain: «Gwil notices and starts accidentally missing his shots.» The clue is the sport: a shot here is a kick or throw at a goal, not a photo or an injection. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence best?
explain: «Give it a shot!» means try. The clue is the phrase «give it», which is about having a go. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of shot. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
explain: Shot is also the past of shoot, as in «She shot the ball into the net.» When you see shot after a helper word like had or was, or in a sentence about something that already happened, it may be a verb. When in doubt, use a dictionary.
fact: Shot can be a noun (a shot, shots) or the past of the verb shoot.
fact: Shot can mean a kick, throw or hit at a goal or basket, as in a shot at goal.
fact: Shot can mean a photograph or a part of a film, as in «a shot of the mountains».
fact: A «flu shot» is an injection of medicine, like a vaccine. «A long shot» means something that is unlikely to work.
fact: Context clues tell you which meaning of shot is needed in each sentence.
exercise: «Before digital cameras, photos were taken on film, so people took fewer, more careful shots.» What does shots mean here? | Injections | Kicks at a goal | *Photographs | Tries
exercise: «Give it a shot!» What does this mean? | *Try | Stop what you are doing | Go to sleep | Throw it away
exercise: Yesterday Sam ___ the ball into the net. Which word fits the gap? | shooting | *shot | shots | shoot
exercise: Ella says the plan is «a long shot». What does she mean? | It is a very long walk | It is sure to work | It is a kind of camera | *It is unlikely to work
test: «Gwil notices and starts accidentally missing his shots.» In this sentence, shots most likely means | Pieces of film | Injections of medicine | Photographs | *Kicks or throws at a goal
test: Mum says, «You need a flu shot before winter.» What is a flu shot? | A pair of football boots | *An injection of medicine, like a vaccine | A long walk outside | A kind of cold drink
exam: Ella says the plan is «a long shot». What does she mean? | It is a kind of camera | It is a very long walk | It is sure to work | *It is unlikely to work
